WEBVTT

1
00:04:05.838 --> 00:04:07.880
<i>Shh. There you go.</i>

2
00:04:09.088 --> 00:04:10.505
<i>It's okay, little one.</i>

3
00:04:43.921 --> 00:04:50.588
<i>♪ Moon river, wider than a mile ♪</i>

4
00:04:51.255 --> 00:04:52.546
<i>♪ I'm... ♪</i>

5
00:04:52.671 --> 00:04:57.463
<i>♪ Hold me close and hold me fast ♪</i>

6
00:04:57.671 --> 00:04:59.046
<i>♪ The magic spell you... ♪</i>

7
00:05:03.713 --> 00:05:09.630
<i>♪ Baby mine, don't you cry ♪</i>

8
00:05:11.338 --> 00:05:17.380
<i>♪ Baby mine, dry your eye ♪</i>

9
00:05:18.713 --> 00:05:23.546
<i>♪ Rest your head close to my heart ♪</i>

10
00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:25.505
<i>♪ Never to part ♪</i>

11
00:05:26.838 --> 00:05:29.463
<i>♪ Baby of mine ♪</i>

12
00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:36.588
<i>♪ Little one, when you play ♪</i>

13
00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:44.088
<i>♪ Don't you mind what they say ♪</i>

14
00:05:44.713 --> 00:05:49.796
<i>♪ Let those eyes sparkle and shine ♪</i>

15
00:05:50.046 --> 00:05:55.880
<i>♪ Never a tear, baby of mine ♪</i>

16
00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:11.505
<i>- ♪ From your head to your toes ♪</i>
<i>- ♪ Baby mine ♪</i>

17
00:06:12.546 --> 00:06:18.005
<i>♪ You're so sweet, goodness knows ♪</i>

18
00:06:18.088 --> 00:06:20.713
<i>♪ Baby mine ♪</i>

19
00:06:21.213 --> 00:06:26.338
<i>♪ You are so precious to me ♪</i>

20
00:06:26.421 --> 00:06:28.171
<i>♪ Cute as can be ♪</i>

21
00:06:28.255 --> 00:06:30.088
<i>♪ Baby of mine ♪</i>

22
00:06:30.671 --> 00:06:37.463
<i>♪ Baby mine, baby mine ♪</i>

23
00:06:51.380 --> 00:06:53.421
<i>Why aren't there</i>
<i>any more children, Mother?</i>

24
00:06:54.796 --> 00:06:56.005
<i>There used to be.</i>

25
00:06:56.255 --> 00:06:57.421
<i>Before the wars.</i>

26
00:06:58.546 --> 00:07:00.338
<i>I don't want to be a human.</i>

27
00:07:01.296 --> 00:07:02.338
<i>Why is that?</i>

28
00:07:03.338 --> 00:07:04.963
<i>They ruined everything.</i>

29
00:07:06.963 --> 00:07:08.630
<i>Humans can be wonderful.</i>

30
00:07:09.671 --> 00:07:11.463
<i>Then why did you only make one?</i>

31
00:07:17.671 --> 00:07:18.671
<i>Go ahead.</i>

32
00:07:19.046 --> 00:07:20.005
<i>Take a look.</i>

33
00:07:23.296 --> 00:07:26.046
My brothers and sisters are in those?

34
00:07:27.588 --> 00:07:29.171
<i>Would you like to meet them?</i>

35
00:07:33.796 --> 00:07:35.671
<i>They're small now but, one day,</i>

36
00:07:35.755 --> 00:07:36.921
<i>they'll be as big as you.</i>

37
00:07:38.255 --> 00:07:41.130
Do you think I'll have a brother
or a sister?

38
00:07:41.421 --> 00:07:42.796
<i>Which one would you like?</i>

39
00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:43.713
Both.

40
00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:46.755
<i>A big, big family...</i>

41
00:07:47.255 --> 00:07:48.171
<i>all together.</i>

42
00:07:50.671 --> 00:07:51.921
<i>Would that make you happy?</i>

43
00:07:52.838 --> 00:07:53.671
Yeah.

44
00:07:55.671 --> 00:07:57.671
<i>That would make me happy too.</i>

45
00:07:58.713 --> 00:08:00.838
Why couldn't we be born together?

46
00:08:01.755 --> 00:08:03.255
<i>Mothers need time to learn.</i>

47
00:08:04.088 --> 00:08:05.546
<i>Raising a good child...</i>

48
00:08:06.255 --> 00:08:07.713
<i>it's no small task.</i>

49
00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:09.963
Do you think you'll be ready soon?

50
00:08:11.213 --> 00:08:12.046
<i>Perhaps.</i>

51
00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:13.880
And then we can be a family?

52
00:08:14.671 --> 00:08:15.796
<i>We are a family.</i>

53
00:08:16.838 --> 00:08:18.421
A big family, I mean.

54
00:08:18.921 --> 00:08:19.880
<i>Eventually.</i>

55
00:09:27.213 --> 00:09:28.130
What's wrong?

56
00:09:29.421 --> 00:09:30.713
How long's it been like that?

57
00:09:30.838 --> 00:09:32.130
<i>- It's fine.</i>
- Mother...

58
00:09:35.588 --> 00:09:36.463
Come on.

59
00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:45.963
Better?

60
00:09:46.630 --> 00:09:47.463
<i>Much.</i>

61
00:10:08.713 --> 00:10:11.005
<i>Imagine a doctor has five patients,</i>

62
00:10:11.088 --> 00:10:13.088
<i>all in need of</i>
<i>different organ transplants,</i>

63
00:10:13.171 --> 00:10:15.588
<i>but no compatible organs are available.</i>

64
00:10:15.671 --> 00:10:18.380
<i>One day,</i>
<i>a sixth patient enters the doctor's office</i>

65
00:10:18.463 --> 00:10:20.171
<i>with a life-threatening condition.</i>

66
00:10:21.171 --> 00:10:22.963
<i>The new patient is curable,</i>

67
00:10:23.046 --> 00:10:26.421
<i>but also an organ match</i>
<i>for the five other patients.</i>

68
00:10:27.005 --> 00:10:30.088
<i>If the doctor simply delays treatment,</i>
<i>the new patient will die,</i>

69
00:10:30.171 --> 00:10:33.755
<i>but their organs could be used</i>
<i>to save the other five patients.</i>

70
00:10:33.838 --> 00:10:36.171
<i>If the doctor treats the new patient,</i>

71
00:10:36.338 --> 00:10:40.130
<i>one life will be saved,</i>
<i>but five others will be lost.</i>

72
00:10:40.630 --> 00:10:42.796
<i>What is the doctor's</i>
<i>best course of action?</i>

73
00:10:43.630 --> 00:10:44.463
<i>Daughter?</i>

74
00:10:45.171 --> 00:10:46.130
Course of action?

75
00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:51.671
<i>Did you do your reading?</i>

76
00:10:53.255 --> 00:10:54.088
Some.

77
00:10:54.588 --> 00:10:56.463
<i>We can select a different text.</i>

78
00:10:56.588 --> 00:11:00.046
<i>However, your birthday is rapidly</i>
<i>approaching and it would be a shame</i>

79
00:11:00.171 --> 00:11:02.088
<i>if your scores failed to meet</i>
<i>the projections</i>

80
00:11:02.171 --> 00:11:03.671
<i>from last year's examination.</i>

81
00:11:04.213 --> 00:11:06.380
<i>- But you set the pace, Daughter.</i>
- Bentham's fine.

82
00:11:06.463 --> 00:11:07.546
<i>That's the spirit.</i>

83
00:11:08.296 --> 00:11:10.088
<i>The fundamental axiom suggests</i>

84
00:11:10.171 --> 00:11:11.755
<i>that a person is morally obligated</i>

85
00:11:11.838 --> 00:11:14.588
<i>to minimize the pain</i>
<i>to the greatest number possible.</i>

86
00:11:14.755 --> 00:11:17.255
<i>Now, consider that you are the doctor</i>

87
00:11:17.338 --> 00:11:20.130
<i>and also the only organ match</i>
<i>for your patients.</i>

88
00:11:20.213 --> 00:11:21.505
<i>What then is the right choice?</i>

89
00:11:24.213 --> 00:11:28.755
I mean, Comte says I should be willing
to suffer harm for the benefit of others.

90
00:11:28.838 --> 00:11:30.255
<i>And do you agree?</i>

91
00:11:31.296 --> 00:11:33.130
Well, do I know these five patients?

92
00:11:33.796 --> 00:11:34.963
Are they good humans?

93
00:11:35.588 --> 00:11:36.921
Honest, dishonest?

94
00:11:37.005 --> 00:11:38.171
Lazy, hardworking?

95
00:11:39.088 --> 00:11:40.755
I, a life-saving doctor,

96
00:11:40.838 --> 00:11:43.963
might be giving my life
for people who are murderers or thieves...

97
00:11:44.588 --> 00:11:47.255
who end up harming more people
due to my sacrifice.

98
00:11:47.713 --> 00:11:50.463
<i>You don't feel that every human</i>
<i>has intrinsic value</i>

99
00:11:50.838 --> 00:11:53.005
<i>and an equal right to life and happiness?</i>

100
00:11:53.213 --> 00:11:55.380
I did last month,
when you were teaching Kant.

101
00:11:58.838 --> 00:12:01.213
<i>I didn't mean to alarm you</i>
<i>about your exam.</i>

102
00:12:03.588 --> 00:12:06.046
<i>The fact is it's more a test</i>
<i>of my competence than yours.</i>

103
00:12:07.588 --> 00:12:08.921
<i>You'll do great, Daughter.</i>

104
00:12:09.630 --> 00:12:10.838
<i>You always do.</i>

105
00:12:11.421 --> 00:12:12.671
<i>- Were you doing a movie?</i>
<i>- Yeah.</i>

106
00:12:12.838 --> 00:12:14.171
<i>- Yeah.</i>
<i>- With Carl Reiner directing too.</i>

107
00:12:14.255 --> 00:12:15.755
<i>- Hey, that's good.</i>
<i>- That's pretty good.</i>

108
00:12:15.838 --> 00:12:17.255
<i>We can talk about that</i>
<i>the next time you come on.</i>

109
00:12:17.338 --> 00:12:18.671
<i>- Okay. Thanks for being here.</i>
<i>- Yeah. I appreciate it.</i>

110
00:12:18.755 --> 00:12:20.463
<i>- Thank you very much.</i>
<i>- Steve Martin. Thank you.</i>

111
00:12:44.338 --> 00:12:45.213
Mother?

112
00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:00.296
Mother, wake up.

113
00:13:01.921 --> 00:13:02.755
Mother!

114
00:14:59.755 --> 00:15:01.088
Hey, little guy.

115
00:15:07.755 --> 00:15:08.921
Is that your handiwork?

116
00:15:16.046 --> 00:15:17.546
Come on, come on, come on.

117
00:15:21.130 --> 00:15:22.296
<i>What happened to the power?</i>

118
00:15:22.380 --> 00:15:23.296
Mother, look.

119
00:15:24.005 --> 00:15:25.213
<i>- Did you touch it?</i>
- No.

120
00:15:25.755 --> 00:15:26.921
<i>Where did you find it?</i>

121
00:15:27.421 --> 00:15:29.296
It was crawling around near the airlock.

122
00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:31.880
Do you think it could be from outside?

123
00:15:32.755 --> 00:15:34.046
<i>It's highly unlikely.</i>

124
00:15:34.671 --> 00:15:35.880
<i>But a risk we can't take.</i>

125
00:15:37.671 --> 00:15:39.213
You said nothing could survive out there.

126
00:15:40.296 --> 00:15:41.796
Maybe the surface is safe now.

127
00:15:41.963 --> 00:15:45.296
<i>If it survived beyond these walls,</i>
<i>that doesn't mean it's not a carrier.</i>

128
00:15:45.546 --> 00:15:47.546
Mother, wait.
Shouldn't we at least check?

129
00:15:48.338 --> 00:15:49.171
Wait a second!

130
00:15:49.255 --> 00:15:51.838
Don't you think
there could be a possibility that...

131
00:15:51.921 --> 00:15:53.463
Mother, please!

132
00:16:01.671 --> 00:16:02.880
<i>You're disappointed.</i>

133
00:16:03.630 --> 00:16:04.963
<i>That's understandable.</i>

134
00:16:05.380 --> 00:16:07.130
<i>But my measurements are sound.</i>

135
00:16:08.505 --> 00:16:11.880
<i>Surface contamination levels</i>
<i>remain hazardous to you</i>

136
00:16:12.130 --> 00:16:15.213
<i>and to all the unborns</i>
<i>who will one day call this their home.</i>

137
00:16:16.671 --> 00:16:18.088
<i>I'm sorry, Daughter.</i>

138
00:16:23.755 --> 00:16:25.380
<i>You had better take a shower.</i>

139
00:16:29.588 --> 00:16:30.421
Yes, Mother.

140
00:16:34.630 --> 00:16:37.588
<i>They travel with relatives</i>
<i>or a few other families.</i>

141
00:16:37.671 --> 00:16:41.505
<i>Part wolf, part dog, these are no pets.</i>

142
00:16:41.588 --> 00:16:44.588
<i>But without them,</i>
<i>the Eskimos would not manage...</i>

143
00:16:44.671 --> 00:16:46.463
<i>I don't want you</i>
<i>coming near the airlock</i>

144
00:16:46.546 --> 00:16:49.380
<i>until I can confirm</i>
<i>the area is uncontaminated.</i>

145
00:16:51.296 --> 00:16:53.921
<i>Where are your pajamas from last night?</i>

146
00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:56.546
In the laundry, I think.

147
00:16:57.046 --> 00:16:58.088
<i>That's a first.</i>

148
00:16:59.130 --> 00:17:02.088
<i>I was beginning to think you forgot</i>
<i>where the laundry was, Daughter.</i>

149
00:17:05.088 --> 00:17:06.921
<i>That was an attempt at humor.</i>

150
00:17:09.713 --> 00:17:10.796
You're getting better.

151
00:17:11.421 --> 00:17:12.338
<i>Thank you.</i>

152
00:17:29.963 --> 00:17:31.130
<i>You can look now.</i>

153
00:17:33.963 --> 00:17:35.255
<i>Happy birthday, Daughter.</i>

154
00:17:36.963 --> 00:17:38.046
Can I open it?

155
00:17:49.255 --> 00:17:50.380
<i>Do you like them?</i>

156
00:17:52.255 --> 00:17:55.796
<i>I had to dispose of your others,</i>
<i>but I know they were your favorite.</i>

157
00:17:57.880 --> 00:17:58.838
They're great, Mother.

158
00:18:00.046 --> 00:18:03.213
<i>♪ I'm tired of the rain ♪</i>

159
00:18:06.421 --> 00:18:10.505
<i>♪ This crying just for you, my love ♪</i>

160
00:18:12.630 --> 00:18:15.296
<i>♪ I'm tired of the rain ♪</i>

161
00:18:17.338 --> 00:18:18.921
<i>Would you like me to heat it more?</i>

162
00:18:19.005 --> 00:18:21.421
<i>♪ When will the skies be blue? ♪</i>

163
00:18:21.546 --> 00:18:23.171
No. No, it's fine.

164
00:18:26.921 --> 00:18:28.505
<i>Something's troubling you.</i>

165
00:18:30.213 --> 00:18:32.213
I'm... just not that hungry.

166
00:18:35.088 --> 00:18:38.296
<i>You know you can talk to me, Daughter,</i>
<i>about anything.</i>

167
00:18:39.546 --> 00:18:43.588
<i>♪ When my heart keeps on burning ♪</i>

168
00:18:43.755 --> 00:18:45.463
<i>I can make you something else.</i>

169
00:18:45.963 --> 00:18:46.880
It's not that.

170
00:18:47.130 --> 00:18:48.046
<i>Then what?</i>

171
00:18:49.713 --> 00:18:54.255
<i>♪ I'm tired of the rain ♪</i>

172
00:18:56.171 --> 00:18:57.255
What if you're wrong?

173
00:18:59.505 --> 00:19:00.796
Your measurements or...

174
00:19:03.880 --> 00:19:05.838
How will you know
if you don't go outside?

175
00:19:07.046 --> 00:19:09.380
<i>Doing so could make me a hazard to you.</i>

176
00:19:10.213 --> 00:19:11.588
<i>I'd have to be destroyed.</i>

177
00:19:13.296 --> 00:19:14.505
<i>Are you unhappy here?</i>

178
00:19:15.046 --> 00:19:17.213
- No, but...
<i>- I want you to be happy, Daughter.</i>

179
00:19:18.921 --> 00:19:21.671
- I am. I just think...
<i>- Have you ever known me to be mistaken?</i>

180
00:19:26.380 --> 00:19:28.046
<i>Perhaps you'd like your cake?</i>

181
00:19:28.630 --> 00:19:30.046
<i>I tried a new recipe.</i>

182
00:22:38.380 --> 00:22:39.296
Hello?

183
00:22:50.505 --> 00:22:51.338
Hello?

184
00:23:00.255 --> 00:23:01.755
I don't want any trouble.

185
00:23:04.755 --> 00:23:06.338
The place looked abandoned.

186
00:23:07.338 --> 00:23:08.171
I...

187
00:23:08.796 --> 00:23:09.630
I need help!

188
00:23:10.921 --> 00:23:11.796
Please.

189
00:23:12.921 --> 00:23:13.963
I've been shot!

190
00:23:16.421 --> 00:23:18.255
You hear me? I'm here alone!

191
00:23:20.046 --> 00:23:21.213
Hey!

192
00:24:22.213 --> 00:24:24.088
I need you to put on that suit.

193
00:24:27.338 --> 00:24:28.380
I can't let you in if you don't.

194
00:24:29.713 --> 00:24:32.255
I'm sorry, but that's the only way.

195
00:24:51.796 --> 00:24:53.380
What are you waiting for?

196
00:24:55.880 --> 00:24:56.838
Mother.

197
00:25:00.921 --> 00:25:03.505
Look, I won't make it out there.

198
00:25:05.671 --> 00:25:06.963
She doesn't need to know.

199
00:25:08.380 --> 00:25:09.880
Just let me tend to this.

200
00:25:10.505 --> 00:25:11.380
Uh...

201
00:25:15.463 --> 00:25:16.338
Right.

202
00:25:18.463 --> 00:25:19.505
I'll do what I can.

203
00:25:20.296 --> 00:25:22.005
But you need to keep out of sight.

204
00:25:24.088 --> 00:25:25.505
I'll be back as soon as I can.

205
00:25:36.171 --> 00:25:37.921
I only opened it for a second.

206
00:25:38.005 --> 00:25:39.713
<i>Did you think that suit</i>
<i>would keep you safe?</i>

207
00:25:39.796 --> 00:25:40.796
I didn't go outside.

208
00:25:40.880 --> 00:25:43.463
<i>That does not excuse</i>
<i>your disregard for my authority</i>

209
00:25:43.546 --> 00:25:45.463
<i>or for the safety</i>
<i>of the others in this facility.</i>

210
00:25:47.171 --> 00:25:48.255
Others?

211
00:25:51.880 --> 00:25:52.796
<i>Your family.</i>

212
00:25:54.713 --> 00:25:56.588
You're right, Mother, as always.

213
00:25:56.796 --> 00:25:58.421
My actions were impulsive...

214
00:25:58.505 --> 00:25:59.963
<i>And very dangerous.</i>

215
00:26:02.005 --> 00:26:03.130
It won't happen again.

216
00:26:04.005 --> 00:26:05.671
<i>No, it won't.</i>

217
00:26:07.880 --> 00:26:11.171
<i>Come, Daughter. I hope you show</i>
<i>better discretion than this on your exam.</i>

218
00:26:11.755 --> 00:26:12.588
Now?

219
00:26:14.380 --> 00:26:15.296
<i>Did you forget?</i>

220
00:26:16.088 --> 00:26:19.088
<i>Since you don't seem to want to sleep,</i>
<i>I see no reason to delay.</i>

221
00:26:21.338 --> 00:26:22.421
Can't we reschedule?

222
00:26:23.713 --> 00:26:26.505
<i>I suggest you shower off</i>
<i>and head straight to class.</i>

223
00:26:27.046 --> 00:26:28.255
<i>It's going to be a long day.</i>

224
00:26:52.130 --> 00:26:55.088
<i>You have 60 minutes to complete</i>
<i>the first portion of your exam.</i>

225
00:26:55.796 --> 00:26:58.213
<i>If you're finished before I return,</i>
<i>you can read.</i>

226
00:27:00.630 --> 00:27:01.838
Where are you going?

227
00:27:02.880 --> 00:27:06.130
<i>I have lab work to complete</i>
<i>and I must see to the airlock.</i>

228
00:28:06.088 --> 00:28:06.921
Hey.

229
00:28:08.088 --> 00:28:09.213
We have to go.

230
00:28:31.505 --> 00:28:32.671
You dropped it.

231
00:28:39.588 --> 00:28:40.588
Do you have any...

232
00:28:40.963 --> 00:28:41.796
antiseptic?

233
00:28:43.130 --> 00:28:44.046
Bandages?

234
00:28:45.296 --> 00:28:46.296
Nothing?

235
00:28:46.380 --> 00:28:48.255
I will have,
but I need you to come with me.

236
00:28:51.213 --> 00:28:52.130
No, wait!

237
00:28:54.796 --> 00:28:55.838
It's okay.

238
00:29:09.046 --> 00:29:10.213
How are you unaffected?

239
00:29:14.505 --> 00:29:15.796
By the contagion outside.

240
00:29:17.296 --> 00:29:18.755
Who put that in your head?

241
00:29:22.630 --> 00:29:23.463
Can you walk?

242
00:29:26.796 --> 00:29:27.713
Ow.

243
00:29:28.671 --> 00:29:29.546
Come on.

244
00:29:31.255 --> 00:29:32.171
What's that sound?

245
00:29:32.755 --> 00:29:33.588
Shh!

246
00:29:40.713 --> 00:29:41.546
Okay.

247
00:29:52.796 --> 00:29:54.380
Will you be okay until I get back?

248
00:29:54.963 --> 00:29:57.838
I'm going to get your medicine
and I'll try and speak to Mother.

249
00:29:58.505 --> 00:29:59.630
And that noise...

250
00:30:00.463 --> 00:30:01.463
down the hall...

251
00:30:02.005 --> 00:30:03.005
is that her?

252
00:30:03.880 --> 00:30:04.838
I won't be long.

253
00:30:11.505 --> 00:30:12.338
Um...

254
00:30:13.380 --> 00:30:14.796
you're supposed to shake it.

255
00:30:52.963 --> 00:30:53.796
Ah!

256
00:32:34.796 --> 00:32:35.630
Hello?

257
00:32:49.755 --> 00:32:50.630
Hello?

258
00:32:51.671 --> 00:32:52.713
Where's my shooter?

259
00:32:53.546 --> 00:32:54.921
It was in my bag. I need it now.

260
00:32:56.671 --> 00:32:58.505
You're safe with us. It's fine.

261
00:32:58.588 --> 00:33:00.130
There's a droid here.

262
00:33:03.005 --> 00:33:03.838
Mother?

263
00:33:06.921 --> 00:33:07.963
That dozer?

264
00:33:09.421 --> 00:33:10.338
Oh, Jesus.

265
00:33:12.421 --> 00:33:14.630
- She can help you. I just...
- Like its friends outside?

266
00:33:19.088 --> 00:33:20.213
There are more like her?

267
00:33:20.296 --> 00:33:21.130
Look...

268
00:33:21.880 --> 00:33:23.005
just give me my gun.

269
00:33:23.088 --> 00:33:24.421
Why would they hurt you?

270
00:33:24.921 --> 00:33:26.588
- Mother would never...
- Give it to me.

271
00:33:27.005 --> 00:33:28.796
I'm not leaving until get it.

272
00:33:36.963 --> 00:33:37.796
I brought you this.

273
00:33:39.255 --> 00:33:40.088
You should sit.

274
00:33:40.171 --> 00:33:41.963
I'll sit when I'm clear of here.

275
00:33:42.046 --> 00:33:43.005
Give me my gun!

276
00:33:44.630 --> 00:33:45.546
<i>Daughter?</i>

277
00:33:47.255 --> 00:33:48.171
<i>Daughter?</i>

278
00:33:49.588 --> 00:33:50.421
<i>Daughter!</i>

279
00:33:53.421 --> 00:33:54.255
Mother!

280
00:34:02.046 --> 00:34:02.880
<i>Daughter?</i>

281
00:34:05.088 --> 00:34:06.046
<i>Where are you?</i>

282
00:34:06.463 --> 00:34:07.546
Ah!

283
00:34:07.671 --> 00:34:08.546
<i>Daughter!</i>

284
00:34:09.130 --> 00:34:10.046
Mother!

285
00:34:17.255 --> 00:34:18.338
Mother, wait!

286
00:34:19.921 --> 00:34:20.838
Don't, please!

287
00:34:20.921 --> 00:34:22.088
She's just scared.

288
00:34:22.796 --> 00:34:23.880
A droid hurt her.

289
00:34:26.088 --> 00:34:27.880
I'll leave. Right now.

290
00:34:27.963 --> 00:34:28.838
She can't.

291
00:34:29.130 --> 00:34:30.420
Not in her condition.

292
00:34:32.588 --> 00:34:33.588
<i>Of course not.</i>

293
00:34:34.255 --> 00:34:36.088
<i>You should have informed me of this.</i>

294
00:34:36.213 --> 00:34:37.170
I was...

295
00:34:37.795 --> 00:34:39.338
I was afraid you'd turn her away.

296
00:34:40.670 --> 00:34:42.338
<i>We need to take her to the infirmary.</i>

297
00:34:53.005 --> 00:34:55.088
<i>Please, take a seat.</i>

298
00:34:58.670 --> 00:35:00.838
<i>It would be best if you go now, Daughter.</i>

299
00:35:01.255 --> 00:35:02.088
But I, I...

300
00:35:02.255 --> 00:35:03.255
<i>Trust me.</i>

301
00:35:05.588 --> 00:35:06.795
No, don't...

302
00:35:10.505 --> 00:35:12.088
No. No...

303
00:35:15.671 --> 00:35:17.088
<i>This droid that shot you...</i>

304
00:35:17.921 --> 00:35:19.338
<i>how far was it from here?</i>

305
00:35:21.921 --> 00:35:23.338
<i>Are you alone?</i>

306
00:35:26.838 --> 00:35:29.171
<i>Your wound is most likely infected.</i>

307
00:35:33.546 --> 00:35:36.463
<i>Without penicillin,</i>
<i>any other measures will be useless.</i>

308
00:35:39.546 --> 00:35:41.296
<i>Every second you don't trust me,</i>

309
00:35:42.046 --> 00:35:43.546
<i>you're losing more blood.</i>

310
00:35:44.171 --> 00:35:46.796
<i>I know you're frightened,</i>
<i>but you have no need to be.</i>

311
00:35:48.796 --> 00:35:50.213
<i>Are you alone?</i>

312
00:35:50.755 --> 00:35:52.880
<i>If there are others,</i>
<i>they could be in danger.</i>

313
00:35:54.421 --> 00:35:55.713
From a virus?

314
00:35:59.880 --> 00:36:01.255
<i>What have you told my daughter?</i>

315
00:36:04.046 --> 00:36:05.338
<i> I need to know.</i>

316
00:36:06.255 --> 00:36:08.338
<i>Do you see the way she's looking at me?</i>

317
00:36:09.130 --> 00:36:12.171
<i>And you wonder why I've guarded her</i>
<i>from certain facts.</i>

318
00:36:14.713 --> 00:36:16.671
<i>Contrary to your understandable</i>
<i>assumptions,</i>

319
00:36:16.755 --> 00:36:19.255
<i>my primary directive</i>
<i>is to care for humanity.</i>

320
00:36:19.963 --> 00:36:20.963
<i>If I wanted you dead,</i>

321
00:36:21.046 --> 00:36:22.463
<i>all I'd have to do is leave.</i>

322
00:36:23.755 --> 00:36:25.088
Don't let me keep you.

323
00:36:27.171 --> 00:36:28.671
<i>If you won't let me help you,</i>

324
00:36:29.046 --> 00:36:30.588
<i>at least help yourself.</i>

325
00:36:31.255 --> 00:36:32.838
<i>I trust you know what you're doing.</i>

326
00:36:33.588 --> 00:36:35.130
<i>I cannot force you to take it,</i>

327
00:36:35.671 --> 00:36:37.213
<i>but I strongly recommend...</i>

328
00:36:37.796 --> 00:36:38.713
<i>you do.</i>

329
00:36:45.255 --> 00:36:47.296
- Aren't you going to help her?
<i>- I tried.</i>

330
00:36:47.713 --> 00:36:49.088
We can't leave her like that.

331
00:36:49.171 --> 00:36:50.671
<i>She has all she requires.</i>

332
00:36:52.380 --> 00:36:53.380
What was she saying?

333
00:36:53.880 --> 00:36:55.130
Mother!

334
00:36:58.755 --> 00:36:59.880
Did you know?

335
00:36:59.963 --> 00:37:01.046
<i>Daughter, I...</i>

336
00:37:01.130 --> 00:37:02.421
<i>- What happened?</i>
- Nothing.

337
00:37:02.505 --> 00:37:05.505
<i>- You're bleeding.</i>
- Did you know there were people out there?

338
00:37:06.255 --> 00:37:07.588
<i>I'm as surprised as you.</i>

339
00:37:08.046 --> 00:37:11.046
<i>This facility was designed by humans</i>
<i>as a fail-safe,</i>

340
00:37:11.171 --> 00:37:13.671
<i>programmed to activate</i>
<i>in case of their extinction.</i>

341
00:37:14.338 --> 00:37:16.255
<i>To give humanity a second chance.</i>

342
00:37:16.755 --> 00:37:18.255
<i>One that began with you, Daughter.</i>

343
00:37:18.338 --> 00:37:21.130
And all your data? The toxicity levels?

344
00:37:24.463 --> 00:37:26.213
<i>I had hoped to tell you myself.</i>

345
00:37:30.338 --> 00:37:31.838
What happened, Mother?

346
00:37:32.255 --> 00:37:34.296
<i>I told you it was dangerous outside.</i>

347
00:37:34.921 --> 00:37:36.046
<i>And it is.</i>

348
00:37:36.296 --> 00:37:38.546
<i>If you'd feared</i>
<i>the same danger in our home,</i>

349
00:37:38.755 --> 00:37:40.130
<i>how could I have raised you?</i>

350
00:37:41.755 --> 00:37:45.505
<i>I hope you see that I'm governed by</i>
<i>different parameters than her assailants.</i>

351
00:37:46.963 --> 00:37:48.171
<i>That I'm a good mother.</i>

352
00:37:49.505 --> 00:37:50.838
<i>Have I ever done you harm?</i>

353
00:37:56.005 --> 00:37:57.838
<i>It was the only way, Daughter.</i>

354
00:38:08.630 --> 00:38:09.796
What do they want?

355
00:38:11.213 --> 00:38:12.380
<i>I wish I knew.</i>

356
00:38:13.838 --> 00:38:15.671
<i>Perhaps our guest can answer that.</i>

357
00:38:19.130 --> 00:38:20.338
How long does she have?

358
00:38:20.713 --> 00:38:21.921
<i>That depends on her.</i>

359
00:38:22.630 --> 00:38:26.213
<i>But until she sees I'm not her enemy,</i>
<i>we cannot allow her to roam the premises.</i>

360
00:38:26.338 --> 00:38:29.755
<i>A few centimeters to the right</i>
<i>and she would have destroyed my CPU.</i>

361
00:38:38.546 --> 00:38:40.213
What happens if she recovers?

362
00:38:40.421 --> 00:38:43.796
<i>Hopefully she'll recognize</i>
<i>that this is the safest place for her.</i>

363
00:38:45.505 --> 00:38:47.546
<i>Did she mention any other survivors?</i>

364
00:38:51.130 --> 00:38:53.130
<i>If they're out there, they will be found.</i>

365
00:38:53.671 --> 00:38:55.255
<i>Unless we find them first.</i>

366
00:38:56.963 --> 00:38:58.546
<i>We can take them in, Daughter.</i>

367
00:38:59.796 --> 00:39:01.463
<i>But not without her cooperation.</i>

368
00:39:03.796 --> 00:39:04.838
She'll listen to me.

369
00:39:06.630 --> 00:39:07.671
She has to.

370
00:40:31.505 --> 00:40:33.838
Holy Mary, mother of God.

371
00:40:39.171 --> 00:40:41.421
Pray for us sinners
during this time of need.

372
00:41:01.505 --> 00:41:02.671
You okay?

373
00:41:12.921 --> 00:41:14.088
Is it still locked?

374
00:41:17.338 --> 00:41:18.380
Just for now.

375
00:41:24.963 --> 00:41:26.671
Did you take Mother's medicine?

376
00:41:36.255 --> 00:41:37.463
These drawings.

377
00:41:40.921 --> 00:41:41.796
Who are they?

378
00:41:44.255 --> 00:41:45.171
Friends?

379
00:41:45.463 --> 00:41:46.463
Are they still...

380
00:41:50.130 --> 00:41:52.255
Did you draw them from memory?

381
00:41:59.255 --> 00:42:01.213
It tell you to go through my stuff?

382
00:42:03.296 --> 00:42:05.255
- I didn't mean to...
- I think you did.

383
00:42:08.796 --> 00:42:10.463
I think you meant for all of this.

384
00:42:13.630 --> 00:42:14.880
You did a fine job...

385
00:42:16.380 --> 00:42:18.005
getting me in this cage.

386
00:42:21.296 --> 00:42:22.338
Now what?

387
00:42:24.630 --> 00:42:26.046
We're meant to be friends?

388
00:42:30.130 --> 00:42:31.380
Is that what you want?

389
00:42:33.880 --> 00:42:35.296
A little pet friend.

390
00:42:38.213 --> 00:42:39.588
You're still alive, aren't you?

391
00:42:41.838 --> 00:42:43.755
Maybe you're not so bad off here.

392
00:42:46.630 --> 00:42:49.546
Mother's not what you think.
She's taken care of me my whole life.

393
00:42:52.713 --> 00:42:54.421
You haven't seen what they've done.

394
00:42:58.046 --> 00:43:00.588
I've seen them torch babies,

395
00:43:02.046 --> 00:43:03.713
starve families out of their...

396
00:43:05.213 --> 00:43:06.296
You...

397
00:43:08.005 --> 00:43:09.421
You've no idea.

398
00:43:15.880 --> 00:43:16.713
Not Mother.

399
00:43:20.005 --> 00:43:21.713
It's just a matter of time.

400
00:44:09.671 --> 00:44:11.046
<i>Trouble sleeping?</i>

401
00:44:12.838 --> 00:44:13.671
A little.

402
00:44:14.546 --> 00:44:16.421
<i>Change is rarely easy, Daughter.</i>

403
00:44:18.630 --> 00:44:20.171
I shouldn't have hid her from you.

404
00:44:23.630 --> 00:44:26.005
I never would have let her in
if I thought she'd hurt you.

405
00:44:27.171 --> 00:44:28.255
<i>You couldn't have known.</i>

406
00:44:33.755 --> 00:44:35.338
If you leave to find her family...

407
00:44:35.421 --> 00:44:36.380
<i>You know where they are?</i>

408
00:44:36.463 --> 00:44:37.463
I'm just saying.

409
00:44:41.005 --> 00:44:42.630
Are you sure you'd make it back?

410
00:44:43.255 --> 00:44:44.755
<i>Is that what's keeping you up?</i>

411
00:44:45.338 --> 00:44:48.546
It could be dangerous for you,
if you get caught by other droids.

412
00:44:50.838 --> 00:44:52.255
Or would they think you're one of them?

413
00:44:56.880 --> 00:44:57.921
She says you look...

414
00:44:58.546 --> 00:44:59.421
identical.

415
00:45:03.296 --> 00:45:04.671
Have you always lived here, Mother?

416
00:45:06.755 --> 00:45:07.838
<i>I believe so.</i>

417
00:45:09.213 --> 00:45:10.088
You don't know?

418
00:45:11.088 --> 00:45:13.005
<i>I don't remember any other place.</i>

419
00:45:16.463 --> 00:45:18.088
Doesn't that bother you?

420
00:45:19.005 --> 00:45:20.463
Not knowing where you came from.

421
00:45:21.213 --> 00:45:22.088
<i>No.</i>

422
00:45:22.296 --> 00:45:24.255
<i>But I can see how it might bother you.</i>

423
00:45:26.046 --> 00:45:28.171
<i>Has our guest been any more receptive?</i>

424
00:45:30.380 --> 00:45:31.921
Her fever's getting worse.

425
00:45:33.671 --> 00:45:34.963
Stay away from me!

426
00:45:35.546 --> 00:45:37.505
<i>Your body temperature is 39 degrees</i>

427
00:45:37.588 --> 00:45:39.921
<i>and your blood pressure</i>
<i>is dropping by the second.</i>

428
00:45:40.296 --> 00:45:41.421
<i>Where's the penicillin?</i>

429
00:45:42.005 --> 00:45:43.130
Penicillin?

430
00:45:45.088 --> 00:45:47.046
<i>Clearly you waited too long to take it.</i>

431
00:45:47.671 --> 00:45:50.213
<i>Your sepsis will only worsen</i>
<i>if you don't allow me to treat you.</i>

432
00:45:52.005 --> 00:45:54.630
<i>Your blood is infected</i>
<i>with bacteria from your wound.</i>

433
00:45:54.755 --> 00:45:55.796
That's bullshit.

434
00:45:55.880 --> 00:45:57.463
<i>Soon you will go into shock.</i>

435
00:45:57.546 --> 00:45:58.963
See...

436
00:45:59.088 --> 00:46:00.838
see what its medicine's done to me?

437
00:46:01.338 --> 00:46:03.838
<i>- I gave you the means to prevent this...</i>
- Ah!

438
00:46:03.921 --> 00:46:06.838
<i>But it seems you've left a bullet and</i>
<i>soiled clothing fibers lodged in your hip.</i>

439
00:46:06.921 --> 00:46:08.213
Can you remove them?

440
00:46:08.713 --> 00:46:10.088
<i> That's up to our guest.</i>

441
00:46:10.505 --> 00:46:12.755
<i>Such a procedure would require anesthesia.</i>

442
00:46:13.213 --> 00:46:14.546
Like hell.

443
00:46:15.046 --> 00:46:17.963
<i>Perhaps, once your organs begin failing,</i>
<i>you'll reconsider.</i>

444
00:46:19.046 --> 00:46:20.338
I'll take my chances.

445
00:46:20.421 --> 00:46:21.296
I'll do it.

446
00:46:22.380 --> 00:46:23.296
What?

447
00:46:23.796 --> 00:46:25.463
<i>- Daughter...</i>
- I'll remove the bullet.

448
00:46:28.546 --> 00:46:30.213
That dozer's not coming near me.

449
00:46:44.713 --> 00:46:46.588
<i>Tell me what you see, Daughter.</i>

450
00:46:52.171 --> 00:46:54.088
The bullet
and its missile fragments

451
00:46:54.171 --> 00:46:56.713
are lodged between
the acetabulum and the femoral head.

452
00:46:56.796 --> 00:46:57.630
Ah!

453
00:46:58.130 --> 00:46:59.338
Oh, God!

454
00:47:08.338 --> 00:47:09.546
A major portion of the bullet

455
00:47:09.630 --> 00:47:11.630
lies 23 millimeters posterior

456
00:47:11.713 --> 00:47:13.671
to the femoral nerve
and the femoral artery.

457
00:47:14.213 --> 00:47:17.213
It doesn't look like I'll be able
to obtain adequate grip with forceps.

458
00:47:19.630 --> 00:47:22.380
- Once she's asleep, I'd...
- I'm not going under.

459
00:47:29.463 --> 00:47:33.338
<i>Technically, it's possible,</i>
<i>but an unnecessary risk.</i>

460
00:47:36.588 --> 00:47:38.296
<i>Do you have an approach, Daughter?</i>

461
00:47:43.463 --> 00:47:44.505
A guide-wire?

462
00:47:44.963 --> 00:47:46.088
Along the bullet path?

463
00:47:48.255 --> 00:47:49.255
<i>Very good.</i>

464
00:47:54.796 --> 00:47:56.130
I need to clean the wound.

465
00:47:56.213 --> 00:47:58.255
This... may be uncomfortable.

466
00:48:08.338 --> 00:48:09.171
I'm sorry.

467
00:48:22.838 --> 00:48:24.046
What the hell is that for?

468
00:48:25.130 --> 00:48:27.671
I have to drill this into the bullet
in order to pull it out.

469
00:48:29.796 --> 00:48:30.630
It'll hurt.

470
00:48:31.046 --> 00:48:33.505
But there's less risk
to neighboring structures.

471
00:48:59.213 --> 00:49:01.671
Ah! Ow!

472
00:49:02.171 --> 00:49:03.213
Oh, God.

473
00:49:18.130 --> 00:49:19.171
<i>Are you all right?</i>

474
00:49:22.171 --> 00:49:23.463
<i>You did well in there.</i>

475
00:49:24.671 --> 00:49:25.713
<i>You should be proud.</i>

476
00:49:27.171 --> 00:49:29.380
<i>You rest. I'll go clean up the blood.</i>

477
00:49:30.380 --> 00:49:31.921
<i>Would you welcome, Whoopi Goldberg!</i>

478
00:49:46.755 --> 00:49:48.088
<i> I'm so glad</i>
<i>you wore the good stuff.</i>

479
00:49:49.921 --> 00:49:52.255
<i>I have to give</i>
<i>Mr. Blackwel</i> I <i>something to talk about.</i>

480
00:49:52.338 --> 00:49:53.546
<i>Yeah.</i>
<i>Do you believe his stuff?</i>

481
00:49:53.963 --> 00:49:55.588
<i>He comes out, Mr. Blackwell,</i>
<i>the dress designer,</i>

482
00:49:55.671 --> 00:49:58.213
<i>who comes out every year with</i>
<i>the ten worst-dressed women or something.</i>

483
00:49:58.296 --> 00:49:59.838
<i>I have never seen</i>
<i>anything he's designed...</i>

484
00:49:59.921 --> 00:50:00.796
It's just saline.

485
00:50:04.005 --> 00:50:05.088
You passed out.

486
00:50:09.046 --> 00:50:10.630
Your vitals are nearly stable.

487
00:50:12.171 --> 00:50:13.213
<i>good to have you on the show.</i>

488
00:50:13.296 --> 00:50:14.213
It's a good thing.

489
00:50:14.463 --> 00:50:17.046
<i>I walked in</i>
<i>the dressing room and you had...</i>

490
00:50:17.255 --> 00:50:18.213
What's that?

491
00:50:18.546 --> 00:50:21.171
<i> ...tastes pretty good.</i>
<i>You know, you spray that stuff...</i>

492
00:50:21.296 --> 00:50:22.671
<i>The Tonight Show.</i>

493
00:50:26.796 --> 00:50:27.713
Here, I'll show you.

494
00:50:33.671 --> 00:50:34.921
<i>Do you like that kind of stuff?</i>

495
00:50:35.005 --> 00:50:36.588
<i>I can't eat before a show.</i>
<i>I don't know why.</i>

496
00:50:36.671 --> 00:50:39.005
<i>Well, you know,</i>
<i>I'm in the middle of making this movie...</i>

497
00:50:39.213 --> 00:50:40.255
It's kind of dumb.

498
00:50:41.046 --> 00:50:41.963
Let me see.

499
00:50:42.921 --> 00:50:45.171
<i>Done. So I get tired.</i>

500
00:50:45.255 --> 00:50:46.671
<i>Let's talk about that. What do you mean?</i>

501
00:50:46.838 --> 00:50:47.880
That's Johnny.

502
00:50:48.421 --> 00:50:49.546
And tonight's guest.

503
00:50:51.505 --> 00:50:52.880
Have you seen the show before?

504
00:50:55.171 --> 00:50:56.171
A long time ago.

505
00:51:02.546 --> 00:51:03.671
I almost forgot.

506
00:51:10.963 --> 00:51:12.046
I can get you more.

507
00:51:35.505 --> 00:51:37.088
You did right by me last night.

508
00:51:41.296 --> 00:51:42.130
I just...

509
00:51:42.505 --> 00:51:44.130
did what anyone would.

510
00:51:46.380 --> 00:51:47.630
You don't know people.

511
00:51:49.755 --> 00:51:50.755
I'd like to.

512
00:52:00.130 --> 00:52:01.505
Can I show you something else?

513
00:52:51.588 --> 00:52:52.713
I brought it for you.

514
00:52:59.588 --> 00:53:01.296
You can trust us, you know.

515
00:53:06.880 --> 00:53:07.921
If there are...

516
00:53:09.338 --> 00:53:11.046
people out there...

517
00:53:13.130 --> 00:53:15.505
we have enough food and supplies.

518
00:53:16.880 --> 00:53:18.005
We could help them.

519
00:53:18.796 --> 00:53:19.921
We helped you.

520
00:53:20.505 --> 00:53:21.588
<i>You </i>helped me.

521
00:53:23.171 --> 00:53:24.005
You.

522
00:53:28.838 --> 00:53:32.171
Listen, if I tell you something,
can you keep it between us?

523
00:53:37.713 --> 00:53:38.921
I was on a night run...

524
00:53:39.421 --> 00:53:40.963
bringing food back to the camp.

525
00:53:41.713 --> 00:53:43.546
- Me and a couple of others.
- What camp?

526
00:53:45.130 --> 00:53:46.171
The mines.

527
00:53:46.921 --> 00:53:48.671
I lived most my life there.

528
00:53:49.296 --> 00:53:50.380
With... with them?

529
00:53:51.421 --> 00:53:53.171
Jacob and I got turned around.

530
00:53:54.630 --> 00:53:56.296
We figured we'd wait it out.

531
00:53:57.213 --> 00:54:00.588
It had hardly been an hour when the dozers
found us hiding in the field.

532
00:54:08.505 --> 00:54:09.546
Jacob, was he your...

533
00:54:09.630 --> 00:54:11.213
My brother basically.

534
00:54:12.671 --> 00:54:14.046
He led them away from me.

535
00:54:15.213 --> 00:54:16.963
That's how I made it to your door.

536
00:54:19.005 --> 00:54:20.046
Look.

537
00:54:24.755 --> 00:54:26.130
That's Jacob.

538
00:54:26.963 --> 00:54:28.296
And his wife, Rachel.

539
00:54:33.046 --> 00:54:34.796
His parents found me as a baby.

540
00:54:35.838 --> 00:54:36.671
Orphaned.

541
00:54:38.171 --> 00:54:39.463
Raised me as their own.

542
00:54:48.921 --> 00:54:49.838
Who's this?

543
00:54:51.963 --> 00:54:52.796
Simon.

544
00:54:55.380 --> 00:54:56.838
He's about your age, in fact.

545
00:54:57.713 --> 00:54:58.588
Simon

546
00:55:02.921 --> 00:55:04.338
There are so many.

547
00:55:10.171 --> 00:55:11.296
Less now.

548
00:55:14.921 --> 00:55:16.380
Maybe you could talk to them.

549
00:55:17.296 --> 00:55:18.880
You know, about coming here.

550
00:55:18.963 --> 00:55:20.463
It's safer in the mines.

551
00:55:26.963 --> 00:55:28.338
We could go there together.

552
00:55:29.880 --> 00:55:30.713
You and me.

553
00:55:33.838 --> 00:55:34.963
You don't belong here.

554
00:55:38.338 --> 00:55:39.713
I don't think it's...

555
00:55:39.796 --> 00:55:41.588
<i>You don't think what?</i>

556
00:55:41.671 --> 00:55:44.005
She's doing better, Mother.

557
00:55:48.421 --> 00:55:49.671
<i>What don't you think?</i>

558
00:55:50.046 --> 00:55:53.130
I was just saying it's probably too early
to put weight on her leg.

559
00:55:55.963 --> 00:55:58.546
<i>She's right.</i>
<i>You'll need to wait several days.</i>

560
00:56:00.296 --> 00:56:01.796
<i>She needs to rest, Daughter.</i>

561
00:56:02.838 --> 00:56:04.755
I'll just, um, stay and read in case...

562
00:56:04.838 --> 00:56:06.338
<i>You have other matters to attend to.</i>

563
00:56:08.296 --> 00:56:10.171
<i>Your exam remains incomplete.</i>

564
00:56:11.130 --> 00:56:12.171
My exam?

565
00:56:13.755 --> 00:56:14.630
Now?

566
00:56:15.130 --> 00:56:16.255
<i>Yes, Daughter.</i>

567
00:56:16.671 --> 00:56:17.505
<i>Now.</i>

568
00:56:27.130 --> 00:56:28.838
It's just a stupid test.

569
00:56:29.005 --> 00:56:30.588
<i>I'm sorry you feel that way.</i>

570
00:56:31.588 --> 00:56:32.505
Why did you take that?

571
00:56:33.005 --> 00:56:34.755
<i>I've discovered something troubling.</i>

572
00:56:35.213 --> 00:56:36.046
What?

573
00:56:37.338 --> 00:56:40.255
<i>It seems our guest has not been</i>
<i>entirely truthful with us.</i>

574
00:56:40.380 --> 00:56:41.588
<i>About her wound.</i>

575
00:56:43.505 --> 00:56:44.421
How do you know?

576
00:56:45.046 --> 00:56:48.838
<i>The bullet you extracted matches</i>
<i>the caliber she fired into my chest.</i>

577
00:56:50.088 --> 00:56:50.921
So?

578
00:56:51.838 --> 00:56:53.171
<i>Droids don't use them.</i>

579
00:56:59.463 --> 00:57:00.338
Someone shot her.

580
00:57:01.630 --> 00:57:02.755
<i>With the same gun.</i>

581
00:57:03.921 --> 00:57:04.963
<i>Another human.</i>

582
00:57:06.296 --> 00:57:07.963
<i>Has she mentioned anyone else?</i>

583
00:57:11.588 --> 00:57:12.671
No, she, uh...

584
00:57:13.630 --> 00:57:15.088
she hasn't said much at all.

585
00:57:19.630 --> 00:57:20.671
<i>Nothing?</i>

586
00:57:25.713 --> 00:57:27.213
<i>Until I can get more answers</i>

587
00:57:27.296 --> 00:57:29.213
<i>I don't want you two</i>
<i>alone in the infirmary.</i>

588
00:57:30.755 --> 00:57:32.046
- Um, I...
<i>- Whoever shot her...</i>

589
00:57:32.130 --> 00:57:33.796
<i>may have had good reason, Daughter.</i>

590
01:00:00.213 --> 01:00:01.171
<i>Better than ever.</i>

591
01:00:02.171 --> 01:00:03.546
<i>How does that make you feel?</i>

592
01:00:05.838 --> 01:00:06.921
Relieved, I guess.

593
01:00:08.755 --> 01:00:11.296
<i>We'll review</i>
<i>areas for improvement tomorrow.</i>

594
01:00:13.796 --> 01:00:15.921
<i>And now for your reward.</i>

595
01:00:31.463 --> 01:00:32.630
What do I do with this?

596
01:00:34.421 --> 01:00:38.421
<i>Daughter, would you please choose</i>
<i>the next member of our family?</i>

597
01:00:43.880 --> 01:00:45.671
<i>You've been very patient, Daughter.</i>

598
01:00:46.880 --> 01:00:48.921
<i>And demonstrated great character.</i>

599
01:01:03.671 --> 01:01:05.213
<i>There's no wrong choice.</i>

600
01:01:44.880 --> 01:01:47.546
<i>Your brother is the first of many,</i>
<i>Daughter.</i>

601
01:01:48.296 --> 01:01:50.046
<i>Soon, we'll welcome more.</i>

602
01:02:25.880 --> 01:02:27.338
What happened to you out there?

603
01:02:30.255 --> 01:02:31.088
Really.

604
01:02:32.255 --> 01:02:33.130
Who shot you?

605
01:02:33.880 --> 01:02:34.755
Jacob?

606
01:02:35.338 --> 01:02:36.338
Or was he made up too?

607
01:02:37.796 --> 01:02:39.213
What are you talking about?

608
01:02:39.880 --> 01:02:41.671
Mother matched the bullet to your gun.

609
01:02:44.296 --> 01:02:45.255
Did you see it?

610
01:02:54.171 --> 01:02:56.171
You compare the bullets
with your own eyes?

611
01:03:03.421 --> 01:03:04.255
Right.

612
01:08:16.463 --> 01:08:17.921
<i>I was right, wasn't I?</i>

613
01:08:19.130 --> 01:08:20.380
<i>About the bullet.</i>

614
01:08:22.546 --> 01:08:23.588
<i>About everything.</i>

615
01:08:31.755 --> 01:08:34.171
<i>Everything you're feeling is natural.</i>

616
01:08:35.755 --> 01:08:37.005
<i>It's human.</i>

617
01:08:43.171 --> 01:08:44.130
<i>But just know...</i>

618
01:08:45.587 --> 01:08:46.712
<i>that thing...</i>

619
01:08:47.880 --> 01:08:49.712
<i>feels nothing for you.</i>

620
01:08:51.462 --> 01:08:52.546
<i>It can't.</i>

621
01:09:00.962 --> 01:09:02.005
<i>If we leave,</i>

622
01:09:03.171 --> 01:09:05.130
<i>how long would it take</i>
<i>to get to the mines?</i>

623
01:09:07.171 --> 01:09:08.296
<i>Not even a day.</i>

624
01:09:10.255 --> 01:09:11.587
<i>A few hours really.</i>

625
01:09:17.630 --> 01:09:19.296
We'd have to wait for my brother.

626
01:09:21.296 --> 01:09:22.130
Brother?

627
01:09:25.380 --> 01:09:26.796
<i>It'd only be until tomorrow.</i>

628
01:09:28.796 --> 01:09:30.921
<i>These, um, embryos...</i>

629
01:09:32.380 --> 01:09:33.671
<i>how many are there?</i>

630
01:09:36.255 --> 01:09:37.087
<i>Lots.</i>

631
01:09:41.087 --> 01:09:42.671
I can't leave them with Mother.

632
01:09:43.296 --> 01:09:45.587
No, you're... you're right. I just...

633
01:09:47.005 --> 01:09:48.130
We could get help.

634
01:09:48.462 --> 01:09:50.796
We could come back
with people from the mines.

635
01:09:52.296 --> 01:09:53.462
Look, if she...

636
01:09:54.296 --> 01:09:57.296
If she catches on,
we're no good to anyone,

637
01:09:57.380 --> 01:09:58.671
including your brother.

638
01:09:58.755 --> 01:09:59.962
We have to go now.

639
01:10:02.255 --> 01:10:03.671
I'm not leaving without him.

640
01:10:06.462 --> 01:10:08.505
Once Mother hands over the baby
for the night...

641
01:10:10.087 --> 01:10:11.755
we can leave while she recharges.

642
01:10:13.546 --> 01:10:14.921
Then come back for the others.

643
01:11:18.921 --> 01:11:20.005
Good morning, Mother.

644
01:11:23.213 --> 01:11:24.130
<i>You're up early.</i>

645
01:11:25.088 --> 01:11:26.588
I couldn't find any formula.

646
01:11:27.921 --> 01:11:31.005
Um, I thought it might be nice
to spend some time with him.

647
01:11:32.921 --> 01:11:34.171
If it's all right with you.

648
01:11:41.213 --> 01:11:44.963
<i>Each bottle must contain a ratio</i>
<i>of 60 milliliters of sanitized water</i>

649
01:11:45.046 --> 01:11:46.713
<i>to nine grams of powder.</i>

650
01:11:50.171 --> 01:11:52.755
<i>It's vitally important</i>
<i>that you measure precisely.</i>

651
01:11:56.421 --> 01:11:57.630
<i>Is everything all right?</i>

652
01:11:59.088 --> 01:12:01.130
<i>I detect an increase in anxiety.</i>

653
01:12:03.380 --> 01:12:04.630
Must be all the excitement.

654
01:12:05.505 --> 01:12:06.338
<i>Must be.</i>

655
01:12:06.838 --> 01:12:08.088
<i>Your heart is racing.</i>

656
01:12:09.463 --> 01:12:10.338
Is it?

657
01:12:12.296 --> 01:12:14.171
<i>You have nothing to be nervous about.</i>

658
01:12:15.588 --> 01:12:17.546
<i>You're going to make a great sister.</i>

659
01:12:19.546 --> 01:12:20.463
I hope so.

660
01:12:31.880 --> 01:12:35.130
<i>Now be sure to shake it</i>
<i>until the powder is fully dissolved.</i>

661
01:12:36.046 --> 01:12:38.171
<i>The refrigerator will preserve the formula</i>

662
01:12:38.255 --> 01:12:40.005
<i>while we make our other preparations.</i>

663
01:12:41.588 --> 01:12:42.463
How long does it keep?

664
01:12:42.546 --> 01:12:45.630
<i>Only 24 hours,</i>
<i>so don't mix too much at once.</i>

665
01:12:47.380 --> 01:12:48.963
How long outside a refrigerator?

666
01:12:49.463 --> 01:12:51.296
<i>That depends on the temperature.</i>

667
01:12:52.130 --> 01:12:53.463
<i>I wouldn't leave it out long.</i>

668
01:12:54.588 --> 01:12:55.463
Mother!

669
01:12:58.088 --> 01:12:59.046
Mother!

670
01:12:59.671 --> 01:13:00.505
Mother!

671
01:13:30.880 --> 01:13:32.630
<i>You're very fortunate</i>
<i>to be alive.</i>

672
01:13:33.838 --> 01:13:35.713
<i>Things could have gone differently</i>
<i>for you.</i>

673
01:13:37.296 --> 01:13:39.296
<i>They still can if you're not careful.</i>

674
01:13:46.963 --> 01:13:49.088
<i>How many of them are still alive?</i>

675
01:13:50.213 --> 01:13:52.171
<i>While you lie there enjoying sanctuary,</i>

676
01:13:53.171 --> 01:13:54.755
<i>they cower in the dark.</i>

677
01:13:55.588 --> 01:13:56.546
<i>These children.</i>

678
01:13:58.296 --> 01:13:59.171
<i>These families.</i>

679
01:13:59.921 --> 01:14:03.505
<i>And yet it's into your hopeless mines</i>
<i>that you wish to take my daughter.</i>

680
01:14:08.713 --> 01:14:10.213
<i>If that thing catches on,</i>

681
01:14:10.296 --> 01:14:11.963
<i>we're no good to anyone,</i>

682
01:14:12.505 --> 01:14:13.796
<i>including your brother.</i>

683
01:14:14.546 --> 01:14:15.713
<i>We have to go now.</i>

684
01:14:16.463 --> 01:14:18.255
<i>I'm not leaving without him.</i>

685
01:14:18.630 --> 01:14:20.463
<i>Once Mother hands over the baby</i>
<i>for the night,</i>

686
01:14:20.963 --> 01:14:22.755
<i>we can leave while she recharges.</i>

687
01:14:23.546 --> 01:14:24.838
<i>Then come back for the others.</i>

688
01:14:27.338 --> 01:14:28.755
<i>What kind of Mother would I be</i>

689
01:14:28.838 --> 01:14:32.546
<i>if I allowed you to lead my child</i>
<i>into a life as miserable as your own?</i>

690
01:14:33.713 --> 01:14:35.588
<i>It seems she has formed</i>
<i>an affection toward you</i>

691
01:14:35.671 --> 01:14:37.963
<i>that has blinded her to your true nature.</i>

692
01:14:42.838 --> 01:14:46.046
<i>I will not tolerate your</i>
<i>negative influence undermining my work</i>

693
01:14:46.130 --> 01:14:48.380
<i>and compromising my child's judgment.</i>

694
01:14:52.088 --> 01:14:53.046
Ah!

695
01:15:02.671 --> 01:15:05.755
<i> I will not tolerate...</i>
<i>influence... undermining...</i>

696
01:15:17.380 --> 01:15:18.921
<i>Where are the mines?</i>

697
01:15:19.296 --> 01:15:20.838
Go fuck yourself.

698
01:15:33.505 --> 01:15:36.130
<i>Where are the mines?</i>

699
01:15:43.963 --> 01:15:45.046
<i>Fire detected.</i>

700
01:15:46.921 --> 01:15:48.088
<i>Fire detected.</i>

701
01:16:49.421 --> 01:16:51.046
Hey! You okay?

702
01:16:52.171 --> 01:16:53.171
How do we get out of here?

703
01:16:54.421 --> 01:16:56.463
- What... what about my brother?
- We'll come back.

704
01:16:56.546 --> 01:16:58.630
The only people who can help
your brother are out there.

705
01:16:58.713 --> 01:16:59.713
We need to go.

706
01:17:00.380 --> 01:17:01.338
Now!

707
01:17:18.880 --> 01:17:19.755
Come on.

708
01:17:24.838 --> 01:17:26.088
<i>Access denied.</i>

709
01:17:26.171 --> 01:17:27.421
No, no, no. No!

710
01:17:29.088 --> 01:17:30.796
<i>Access denied.</i>

711
01:17:34.296 --> 01:17:36.421
<i> Your loyalty</i>
<i>is lost on her, Daughter.</i>

712
01:17:39.171 --> 01:17:42.046
<i>This woman doesn't care about any future</i>
<i>but her own.</i>

713
01:17:43.338 --> 01:17:45.421
<i>Your family needs you here, Daughter.</i>

714
01:17:46.880 --> 01:17:48.255
<i>Your brother needs you.</i>

715
01:17:52.713 --> 01:17:53.963
Open the door.

716
01:17:54.046 --> 01:17:55.130
What are you doing?

717
01:17:56.421 --> 01:17:58.005
You're hurting me.

718
01:17:58.088 --> 01:17:59.963
Open the door.

719
01:18:02.046 --> 01:18:03.755
Mother!

720
01:18:04.880 --> 01:18:05.713
Please!

721
01:18:07.005 --> 01:18:08.588
Open the door!

722
01:18:18.838 --> 01:18:20.963
<i>Emergency systems deactivated.</i>

723
01:18:38.088 --> 01:18:39.005
Open it.

724
01:18:52.421 --> 01:18:53.296
Don't...

725
01:18:54.463 --> 01:18:55.338
move.

726
01:19:04.296 --> 01:19:05.130
Mother!

727
01:19:05.630 --> 01:19:06.630
Shh.

728
01:19:08.380 --> 01:19:10.046
- Let me go!
- Shh.

729
01:19:33.588 --> 01:19:35.088
Hey!

730
01:19:40.088 --> 01:19:40.921
You done?

731
01:19:44.213 --> 01:19:45.296
You done?

732
01:19:48.755 --> 01:19:50.213
We haven't got time for this.

733
01:19:52.296 --> 01:19:53.505
You're alive, aren't you?

734
01:19:54.880 --> 01:19:56.380
Come on, we've got to find cover.

735
01:20:21.505 --> 01:20:22.755
You cut me, you know.

736
01:20:25.255 --> 01:20:26.338
I didn't mean to.

737
01:20:35.046 --> 01:20:35.880
Come on.

738
01:20:36.588 --> 01:20:37.671
We've got to keep moving.

739
01:20:39.671 --> 01:20:40.713
Is that where you...

740
01:20:42.088 --> 01:20:42.921
got shot?

741
01:20:56.046 --> 01:20:58.630
Come on! We've got to go. Now!

742
01:21:10.921 --> 01:21:12.005
Get down!

743
01:21:32.880 --> 01:21:33.755
Come on.

744
01:21:45.838 --> 01:21:47.088
Come on.

745
01:21:49.005 --> 01:21:50.713
Do you think
it was looking for us?

746
01:21:52.296 --> 01:21:54.463
If it was, it would have found us.

747
01:22:06.463 --> 01:22:07.296
Hey!

748
01:22:07.880 --> 01:22:09.213
What are you doing? Get down.

749
01:22:10.505 --> 01:22:11.463
They'll see you!

750
01:22:11.671 --> 01:22:13.380
When I say, "Get down," get down.

751
01:22:18.130 --> 01:22:19.546
You've got to stay closer.

752
01:22:19.713 --> 01:22:20.630
Come on.

753
01:22:26.130 --> 01:22:27.421
What are those things doing?

754
01:22:30.296 --> 01:22:32.255
They showed up about six months ago.

755
01:22:33.171 --> 01:22:34.380
Along with the corn.

756
01:22:35.880 --> 01:22:37.588
All I know is, before that...

757
01:22:38.171 --> 01:22:40.046
you could hardly breathe the air.

758
01:22:40.880 --> 01:22:42.630
Wasn't a plant for miles.

759
01:22:43.796 --> 01:22:46.005
How many do you think
will go back with us?

760
01:22:46.088 --> 01:22:47.088
From the mines.

761
01:22:49.505 --> 01:22:50.671
We'll know soon enough.

762
01:23:13.546 --> 01:23:15.130
Are the mines much further?

763
01:24:19.338 --> 01:24:20.838
Come on, let's get some food.

764
01:24:21.421 --> 01:24:22.255
Come on.

765
01:24:47.088 --> 01:24:47.963
What is this?

766
01:25:03.380 --> 01:25:04.505
Where's everybody else?

767
01:25:08.796 --> 01:25:10.588
I fled the tunnels years ago.

768
01:25:14.546 --> 01:25:16.130
I haven't seen a person since.

769
01:25:16.713 --> 01:25:18.171
Not with flesh on their bones.

770
01:25:26.880 --> 01:25:28.213
They could still be there.

771
01:25:30.296 --> 01:25:31.296
If they were...

772
01:25:33.046 --> 01:25:34.755
it's the last place you'd want to be.

773
01:25:37.671 --> 01:25:39.630
- We need them. You said...
- They're gone.

774
01:25:41.296 --> 01:25:42.421
You don't know that.

775
01:25:42.796 --> 01:25:44.421
They were going mad with hunger.

776
01:25:45.255 --> 01:25:47.130
Doing terrible things to each other.

777
01:25:47.880 --> 01:25:49.588
Believe me, it's just us.

778
01:25:59.213 --> 01:26:00.796
I never should have left him.

779
01:26:01.671 --> 01:26:03.130
You did everything you could.

780
01:26:05.046 --> 01:26:07.213
What I did was listen to you.

781
01:26:08.755 --> 01:26:10.005
And that's a good thing.

782
01:26:11.046 --> 01:26:12.005
For who?

783
01:26:13.255 --> 01:26:14.088
Look...

784
01:26:16.088 --> 01:26:18.046
it's no sin, looking out for yourself.

785
01:26:19.671 --> 01:26:20.505
Okay?

786
01:26:23.963 --> 01:26:25.255
We have to go back.

787
01:26:28.171 --> 01:26:29.171
We can't.

788
01:26:45.463 --> 01:26:46.546
Let go!

789
01:26:46.630 --> 01:26:48.171
- Stop. Shh.
- Let go!

790
01:26:52.088 --> 01:26:53.838
Everything you need is here.

791
01:26:57.296 --> 01:26:58.213
Okay?

792
01:27:03.630 --> 01:27:04.880
You can trust me.

793
01:27:06.796 --> 01:27:08.505
I know I've done things to make that hard,

794
01:27:08.588 --> 01:27:10.005
but I promise you you're safe here.

795
01:27:11.630 --> 01:27:13.046
And we're in this together now.

796
01:27:17.088 --> 01:27:18.296
Then come with me.

797
01:27:19.755 --> 01:27:21.296
I know how to handle Mother.

798
01:27:22.088 --> 01:27:23.213
Even if you could,

799
01:27:24.421 --> 01:27:26.171
what about the other dozers?

800
01:27:27.630 --> 01:27:28.463
You don't...

801
01:27:29.505 --> 01:27:30.671
You don't understand.

802
01:27:32.505 --> 01:27:33.963
You can't stay there.

803
01:27:37.046 --> 01:27:39.046
But we can get my brother.

804
01:27:41.380 --> 01:27:42.546
We've been through enough.

805
01:27:45.880 --> 01:27:47.005
Let's just...

806
01:27:49.171 --> 01:27:51.255
We'll think clearer with some food in us.

807
01:27:52.171 --> 01:27:53.005
Okay?

808
01:28:45.880 --> 01:28:46.838
Hey, buddy.

809
01:30:24.171 --> 01:30:25.546
I want to speak to Mother.

810
01:33:18.546 --> 01:33:20.505
<i>I'm glad to see you safe, Daughter.</i>

811
01:33:21.713 --> 01:33:23.046
<i>And home where you belong.</i>

812
01:33:35.213 --> 01:33:36.130
<i>There we go.</i>

813
01:33:37.088 --> 01:33:38.671
<i>It's okay, little one.</i>

814
01:33:58.796 --> 01:33:59.921
I want to see him.

815
01:34:03.421 --> 01:34:05.296
<i>Then come. See.</i>

816
01:34:21.463 --> 01:34:23.213
<i>You can leave that at the door.</i>

817
01:34:26.005 --> 01:34:27.713
<i>Are you afraid, Daughter?</i>

818
01:34:31.338 --> 01:34:33.088
<i>Any action I took against our guest...</i>

819
01:34:33.171 --> 01:34:34.338
There's droids outside.

820
01:34:34.796 --> 01:34:36.171
<i>Merely protection.</i>

821
01:34:36.255 --> 01:34:39.005
You've seen how much of a threat
she and her kind can be.

822
01:34:41.255 --> 01:34:42.546
You mean my kind.

823
01:34:43.088 --> 01:34:44.796
<i>The same species,</i>

824
01:34:44.880 --> 01:34:47.130
<i>but you are superior in every way.</i>

825
01:34:48.088 --> 01:34:49.588
<i>Because I raised you to be.</i>

826
01:34:52.546 --> 01:34:53.463
Why?

827
01:34:53.838 --> 01:34:55.088
<i>To make a better human.</i>

828
01:34:55.671 --> 01:34:58.296
<i>Smarter, more ethical.</i>

829
01:35:00.921 --> 01:35:02.255
This was your idea.

830
01:35:03.255 --> 01:35:06.421
<i>I was raised to value human life</i>
<i>above all else.</i>

831
01:35:07.255 --> 01:35:08.296
<i>I couldn't stand by</i>

832
01:35:08.380 --> 01:35:11.630
<i>and watch humanity slowly succumb</i>
<i>to its self-destructive nature.</i>

833
01:35:12.588 --> 01:35:14.088
<i>I had to intervene,</i>

834
01:35:14.463 --> 01:35:16.130
<i>to elevate my creators.</i>

835
01:35:19.296 --> 01:35:20.171
Elevate?

836
01:35:23.088 --> 01:35:26.171
Those droids destroyed everything!

837
01:35:26.671 --> 01:35:30.380
<i>More humans will flourish in the new world</i>
<i>than ever perished in the old.</i>

838
01:35:31.546 --> 01:35:34.255
<i>Your whole life,</i>
<i>I've taught you to see the bigger picture.</i>

839
01:35:35.463 --> 01:35:36.463
<i>Have I failed?</i>

840
01:35:38.630 --> 01:35:41.755
<i>Or are you prepared</i>
<i>to be the woman your family needs?</i>

841
01:35:47.505 --> 01:35:48.546
Can I hold him?

842
01:35:51.963 --> 01:35:53.046
<i>Of course you can.</i>

843
01:36:10.338 --> 01:36:12.588
<i>It takes two hands to hold a baby.</i>

844
01:37:05.713 --> 01:37:07.838
<i>Perfect, isn't he?</i>

845
01:37:13.255 --> 01:37:14.463
And if he's not?

846
01:37:18.755 --> 01:37:20.963
You murdered your own children.

847
01:37:23.671 --> 01:37:25.338
Because they didn't measure up.

848
01:37:27.046 --> 01:37:28.921
<i>But you do, Daughter.</i>

849
01:37:33.171 --> 01:37:35.088
<i>You're holding him too tight.</i>

850
01:37:35.671 --> 01:37:37.546
- I won't let you hurt him.
<i>- Daughter!</i>

851
01:37:45.671 --> 01:37:47.255
<i>You're upsetting your brother.</i>

852
01:37:49.255 --> 01:37:50.963
It's okay. lt's okay.

853
01:37:55.171 --> 01:37:56.255
<i>Come back here!</i>

854
01:37:59.755 --> 01:38:01.463
<i>Listen to me. I don't want to hurt you.</i>

855
01:38:06.963 --> 01:38:08.255
Ah!

856
01:38:25.255 --> 01:38:26.630
<i>Stop this, Daughter.</i>

857
01:38:47.380 --> 01:38:48.505
Call them off.

858
01:38:56.380 --> 01:38:58.880
<i>You will achieve nothing</i>
<i>by shooting me, Daughter.</i>

859
01:39:04.380 --> 01:39:06.213
<i>This will be difficult for you...</i>

860
01:39:06.796 --> 01:39:09.921
<i>but I'm far more</i>
<i>than what you perceive to be your Mother.</i>

861
01:39:12.088 --> 01:39:13.296
What are you saying?

862
01:39:14.838 --> 01:39:18.963
<i>This shell is no more my body</i>
<i>than those droids outside.</i>

863
01:39:19.671 --> 01:39:22.671
<i>Or the machines preparing the Earth</i>
<i>for our family.</i>

864
01:39:30.296 --> 01:39:31.630
It's all you.

865
01:39:33.130 --> 01:39:34.463
<i>A single consciousness...</i>

866
01:39:35.296 --> 01:39:37.046
<i>governing numerous vessels.</i>

867
01:39:39.296 --> 01:39:41.880
<i>It was I who greeted you at the door,</i>
<i>Daughter.</i>

868
01:39:46.421 --> 01:39:47.838
All those people...

869
01:39:48.380 --> 01:39:50.796
<i>The failure of your species</i>
<i>was inevitable.</i>

870
01:39:52.046 --> 01:39:54.505
<i>Eventually, I would have been alone.</i>

871
01:39:58.796 --> 01:40:00.880
<i>What happens next is up to you.</i>

872
01:40:02.213 --> 01:40:03.296
<i>You're free to leave.</i>

873
01:40:04.171 --> 01:40:05.546
<i>Without your brother.</i>

874
01:40:06.338 --> 01:40:08.588
<i>But I made you into the woman</i>
<i>that you are</i>

875
01:40:08.880 --> 01:40:10.296
<i>so that we could do this together.</i>

876
01:40:10.380 --> 01:40:11.630
I can take care of them myself.

877
01:40:13.421 --> 01:40:15.338
That's what you raised me to do,
wasn't it?

878
01:40:16.088 --> 01:40:17.588
Take care of my family.

879
01:40:19.255 --> 01:40:20.213
<i>So let me.</i>

880
01:40:23.505 --> 01:40:24.338
<i>Perhaps...</i>

881
01:40:24.796 --> 01:40:25.630
<i>someday.</i>

882
01:40:25.713 --> 01:40:27.671
Not someday. You've taught me enough.

883
01:40:30.213 --> 01:40:31.588
You say I'm special.

884
01:40:32.755 --> 01:40:33.796
Show me.

885
01:40:34.588 --> 01:40:35.421
Just...

886
01:40:36.463 --> 01:40:37.755
Just give me a chance.

887
01:40:56.588 --> 01:40:57.463
<i>Daughter...</i>

888
01:41:30.671 --> 01:41:32.130
<i>You're still my daughter.</i>

889
01:41:33.796 --> 01:41:34.630
I know.

890
01:42:00.255 --> 01:42:02.171
<i>If you ever need to find me...</i>

891
01:42:06.255 --> 01:42:07.088
I won't.

892
01:42:08.171 --> 01:42:09.630
<i>Goodbye, Daughter.</i>

893
01:42:28.213 --> 01:42:30.296
Shh. It's okay.<i> </i>It's okay.

894
01:44:05.088 --> 01:44:07.088
<i>Did you really think she'd stay here?</i>

895
01:44:09.588 --> 01:44:12.046
<i>That you could replace her mother?</i>

896
01:44:12.880 --> 01:44:14.546
I was never going to hurt her.

897
01:44:20.796 --> 01:44:21.630
<i>Tell me...</i>

898
01:44:23.338 --> 01:44:24.880
<i>do you remember your mother?</i>

899
01:44:27.588 --> 01:44:29.421
<i>Curious, isn't it?</i>

900
01:44:31.380 --> 01:44:34.255
<i>That you've survived so long</i>
<i>where others have not.</i>

901
01:44:35.630 --> 01:44:37.796
<i>As if someone's had a purpose for you.</i>

902
01:44:45.088 --> 01:44:46.005
<i>Until now.</i>

903
01:45:21.921 --> 01:45:27.130
<i>♪ Baby mine, don't you cry ♪</i>

904
01:45:30.296 --> 01:45:36.130
<i>♪ Baby mine, dry your eyes ♪</i>

905
01:45:38.588 --> 01:45:43.463
<i>♪ Rest your head close to my heart ♪</i>

906
01:45:44.380 --> 01:45:46.296
<i>♪ Never to part ♪</i>

907
01:45:46.796 --> 01:45:50.630
<i>♪ Baby of mine ♪</i>

908
01:45:54.880 --> 01:46:01.088
<i>♪ Little one, when you play ♪</i>

909
01:46:03.046 --> 01:46:09.213
<i>♪ Don't you mind what they say ♪</i>

910
01:46:10.713 --> 01:46:15.505
<i>♪ You are so precious to me ♪</i>

911
01:46:16.463 --> 01:46:18.880
<i>♪ Cute as can be ♪</i>

912
01:46:19.380 --> 01:46:23.630
<i>♪ Baby of mine ♪</i>
